<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- Hardened-runtime entitlements for Tilo.app (Tilo and the updater;
     tilo-runtime adds its two capture devices in Runtime.entitlements).
     Deliberately empty: every exception below was considered and is unused.

     - com.apple.security.app-sandbox: absent. tilo-runtime is the launcher
       that confines apps (App Sandbox or Seatbelt via launcher-macos); it
       spawns /usr/bin/sandbox-exec and must reach the user's files, which
       App Sandbox would forbid. Without App Sandbox the network.client and
       network.server entitlements have no effect, so they are absent too.
     - com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit and allow-unsigned-executable-memory:
       absent. Neither binary links a JIT (no wasmtime, V8 or webview engine
       in either dependency graph); rendering is wgpu on Metal.
     - com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation: absent. Both binaries
       are statically linked Rust; the store's `thin` feature
       (runtime-dylib) is not built for this bundle, and ash's Vulkan loader
       is reached only through the Linux DMA-BUF import.
     - com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables: absent. Apps
       receive their environment from launcher-macos, not through dyld.
     - com.apple.security.get-task-allow: absent. It is a debugging exception
       that notarization rejects. -->
<plist version="1.0"><dict/></plist>
